IMPORT prelude

-- Women's Charter 1961 (Singapore) -- when a marriage is void (ss 9, 11, 11A, 12, 13), marrying again during a spouse's
-- lifetime (s 6A), parental consent for under-21s and the licence waiting period (ss 17(2), 21A), the notice of marriage
-- and its lapse (ss 14, 15), who solemnises and how (ss 22, 23, 40; added for REQ-0005 and REQ-0006), maintenance of a wife,
-- an incapacitated husband and children (s 69), protection orders against family violence (ss 60, 60A, 63C), and
-- divorce: jurisdiction, the three-year bar and irretrievable breakdown (ss 93, 94, 95, 95A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation "version in
-- force from 17/8/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/WC1961.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the
-- deposit is Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it governs who may marry, the
-- duty to maintain a spouse and children, protection from family violence, and divorce. (An automated count found 0 of
-- the 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by its slug title; that count undercounts Acts cited by short titles.)
-- SCOPED, because the Act is several hundred pages. Not encoded: the prohibited degrees (s 10, First Schedule), the
-- Second Schedule list of whose consent is needed, the declarations and licence conditions (ss 16, 18), caveats (ss 19, 20),
-- special licences (s 21), remote solemnisation conditions (s 24) beyond a flag, registration (Part 4), the family violence assessment and
-- enforcement powers (ss 58-66), maintenance enforcement (ss 71 onward), custody, division of matrimonial assets and
-- post-divorce maintenance (Part 10), judicial separation and nullity procedure, the Part 10A mediation and parenting
-- programmes, married women's property, and Parts on women and girls.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Women's Charter 1961 -- marriage, maintenance, family violence and divorce`

§§ `9, 11, 11A, 12, 13 -- void marriages`

-- s 9: a marriage "between persons either of whom is below 18 years of age is void unless the solemnisation of the
-- marriage was authorised by a special marriage licence".
-- s 11: void if either party "at the date of the marriage, is married under any law, religion, custom or usage to any
-- other person".
-- s 11A(1): a marriage solemnised on or after 1 October 2016 is void if a party enters it knowing or having reason to
-- believe "that the purpose of the marriage is to assist ... to obtain an immigration advantage" AND gratification is
-- offered, given or received as an inducement; (2) not void if "both parties ... believed on reasonable grounds" it
-- would result in "a genuine marital relationship".
-- s 12(1): void between persons who "are not respectively male and female".
-- s 13: a marriage solemnised in Singapore is void unless solemnised (a) on a valid marriage licence or special marriage
-- licence and (b) by the Registrar or a licensed solemniser.
-- The prohibited degrees (s 10) are not encoded. The 1 October 2016 start date of s 11A is not modelled.
DECLARE Marriage HAS
    `age of the younger party` IS A NUMBER
    `authorised by a special marriage licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party was already married` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties are male and female` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered to obtain an immigration advantage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gratification was given as an inducement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both reasonably believed it genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `solemnised in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by the Registrar or a licensed solemniser` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the marriage` IS A Marriage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the marriage is void` IF
        (`the marriage`'s `age of the younger party` < 18 AND (NOT `the marriage`'s `authorised by a special marriage licence`))
    OR  `the marriage`'s `a party was already married`
    OR  (NOT `the marriage`'s `the parties are male and female`)
    OR  (`the marriage`'s `entered to obtain an immigration advantage`
            AND `the marriage`'s `gratification was given as an inducement`
            AND (NOT `the marriage`'s `both reasonably believed it genuine`))
    OR  (`the marriage`'s `solemnised in Singapore`
            AND ((NOT `the marriage`'s `on a valid licence`) OR (NOT `the marriage`'s `by the Registrar or a licensed solemniser`)))

§§ `6A -- marrying again during the lifetime of a husband or wife`

-- s 6A: "Whoever, having a husband or wife living, marries in any case in which such marriage is void by reason of its
-- taking place during the life of such husband or wife" -- (a) if the offender concealed the former marriage from the
-- new spouse, imprisonment up to 10 years "and shall also be liable to" a fine up to $15,000; (b) otherwise up to
-- 7 years and $10,000.
-- Exceptions: not where the earlier marriage "has been declared void by a court of competent jurisdiction", nor where
-- the earlier spouse "has been continually absent from such person for a period of 7 years, and has not been heard of
-- by such person as being alive within that time", PROVIDED the person "informs the person with whom the marriage is
-- contracted, of the real state of facts".
GIVEN `has a living spouse` IS A BOOLEAN, `earlier marriage declared void by a court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years the spouse has been continually absent` IS A NUMBER, `heard of the spouse as alive within that time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `told the new partner the real facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `marrying again is an offence` IF
        `has a living spouse`
    AND (NOT `earlier marriage declared void by a court`)
    AND (NOT (`years the spouse has been continually absent` >= 7
              AND (NOT `heard of the spouse as alive within that time`)
              AND `told the new partner the real facts`))

GIVEN `concealed the former marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment for marrying again in years` IS
    IF `concealed the former marriage` THEN 10 ELSE 7

GIVEN `concealed the former marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for marrying again` IS
    IF `concealed the former marriage` THEN 15000 ELSE 10000

§§ `17(2), 21A -- the marriage licence`

-- s 17(2): a marriage licence "must be issued (a) after the expiry of 21 days from the date of the notice of marriage;
-- and (b) before the notice of marriage ceases to have effect". s 15(1)(a): the notice ceases to have effect when
-- "3 months (or any longer prescribed period) have elapsed" without solemnisation, or on cancellation.
-- INFERENCE: "after the expiry of 21 days" is read as from day 22 onward, counting the notice date as day 0.
GIVEN `days since the notice of marriage` IS A NUMBER, `the notice has ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence may be issued` IF
    `days since the notice of marriage` > 21 AND (NOT `the notice has ceased to have effect`)

-- s 21A(1): the Registrar "must not issue a marriage licence for the marriage of a minor" unless, for each person in
-- the Second Schedule, that person consents, the court consents in lieu, or the Registrar dispenses with it.
-- (4): not for a minor who was previously in a dissolved or annulled marriage, or is a widower or widow.
-- (5): "minor" means "a person who is below 21 years of age". (Not 18: the voidness age in s 9.)
GIVEN `the age of the party` IS A NUMBER, `previously married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consents are needed before a licence` IF
    `the age of the party` < 21 AND (NOT `previously married`)

§§ `14, 15 -- the notice of marriage and when it lapses`

-- REQ-0005 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl, cradle-to-grave-simone e052): notice given 20 April 2029; earliest
-- solemnisation, and when the notice lapses.
-- s 14(1): one party "must give to the Registrar a notice of marriage". s 15(1): the notice "ceases to have effect if --
-- (a) 3 months (or any longer prescribed period) have elapsed since the notice of marriage was given to the Registrar and
-- the intended marriage has not been solemnised; or (b) the notice of marriage is cancelled by the Registrar". (3): if it
-- ceases, "any marriage licence issued in consequence of that notice of marriage is void" and "a fresh notice of marriage
-- must be given before the parties may lawfully marry".
-- s 13 (above) and s 17(2) (below): a marriage needs a valid licence, and a licence issues only "after the expiry of 21
-- days from the date of the notice". Counting the notice date as day 0 (Interpretation Act s 50(a)), the earliest licence,
-- and so the earliest solemnisation, is day 22: for a notice on 20 April 2029, 12 May 2029. REQ-0005 expected "21 days after
-- notice" (11 May); the text gives one day later.
-- INFERENCE: "3 months ... have elapsed" is read as reached on the same day of the month three months on (a notice of
-- 20 April 2029 ceases on 20 July 2029). A notice given on a day with no counterpart three months on (31 May -> 31 August
-- exists, but 30 November -> 30 February does not) is not modelled: the function returns that day number regardless.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earliest solemnisation, in days after the notice` MEANS 22

GIVEN `notice year` IS A NUMBER, `notice month` IS A NUMBER, `notice day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date the notice lapses, as YYYYMMDD` MEANS
    IF `notice month` PLUS 3 GREATER THAN 12
    THEN (`notice year` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS (`notice month` PLUS 3 MINUS 12) TIMES 100 PLUS `notice day`
    ELSE `notice year` TIMES 10000 PLUS (`notice month` PLUS 3) TIMES 100 PLUS `notice day`

GIVEN `months elapsed since the notice` IS A NUMBER, `cancelled by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN, `already solemnised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice has ceased to have effect` IF
        (NOT `already solemnised`)
    AND (`months elapsed since the notice` AT LEAST 3 OR `cancelled by the Registrar`)

§§ `22, 23, 40 -- who solemnises, and how`

-- REQ-0006 (cradle-to-grave-simone e053): who may solemnise at the Registry of Marriages, and what makes it valid.
-- s 22(1): "A marriage may be solemnised by the Registrar or a licensed solemniser." s 23(1): it "must be solemnised with all
-- the following persons in the presence of each other in Singapore: (a) the parties ...; (b) the Registrar or a licensed
-- solemniser; (c) at least 2 credible witnesses", unless (s 24) the Registrar permits remote solemnisation by live video.
-- (2): the solemniser "must not solemnise the marriage unless ... satisfied that both parties freely consent".
-- s 13: the marriage is VOID unless on a valid licence and by the Registrar or a licensed solemniser. Missing witnesses are
-- NOT a ground in s 13: s 40(1)(b) makes it an offence for the solemniser who "knowingly ... solemnises ... without at
-- least 2 credible witnesses" (3 years and a fine up to $5,000), and the Act as read does not make the marriage void for it.
-- REQ-0006 expected the witnesses as a condition of validity; on the words of s 13 they are a condition of lawful
-- solemnisation, not of validity.
DECLARE Officiant IS ONE OF
    `the Registrar`
    `a licensed solemniser`
    `a religious leader without a solemniser's licence`
    `a friend of the couple`

GIVEN `the officiant` IS AN Officiant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officiant may solemnise a marriage` IF
    CONSIDER `the officiant`
    WHEN `the Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licensed solemniser` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Solemnisation HAS
    `the officiant` IS AN Officiant
    `on a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `witnesses present` IS A NUMBER
    `all present together or remote with permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both parties freely consented` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Solemnisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ceremony is void under section 13` IF
        (NOT `the ceremony`'s `on a valid licence`)
    OR  (NOT `the officiant may solemnise a marriage` (`the ceremony`'s `the officiant`))

GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Solemnisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ceremony meets section 23` IF
        `the ceremony`'s `witnesses present` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the ceremony`'s `all present together or remote with permission`
    AND `the ceremony`'s `both parties freely consented`

GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Solemnisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the solemniser commits a section 40 offence` IF
        (NOT `the ceremony`'s `on a valid licence`)
    OR  `the ceremony`'s `witnesses present` LESS THAN 2

§§ `69 -- maintenance of a wife, an incapacitated husband and children`

-- s 69(1): the court may, "on the application of a wife, and on due proof that her husband has neglected or refused to
-- provide reasonable maintenance for her", order maintenance. (1A): the same for "an incapacitated husband" against his
-- wife. s 2: "incapacitated husband" -- during the marriage is or becomes incapacitated by disability or illness from
-- earning a livelihood and unable to maintain himself, and continues to be unable to maintain himself.
-- A husband who is not incapacitated has no claim under s 69.
DECLARE Spouse IS ONE OF
    `a wife`
    `an incapacitated husband`
    `a husband who is not incapacitated`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A Spouse, `the other spouse neglected or refused reasonable maintenance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order spousal maintenance` IF
    `the other spouse neglected or refused reasonable maintenance` AND
    CONSIDER `the applicant`
    WHEN `a husband who is not incapacitated` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 69(3): an application for a child may be made by (a) a guardian or person with actual custody; (b) "where the child
-- has attained 21 years of age, by the child himself or herself"; (c) where the child is below 21, any sibling who has
-- attained 21; or (d) a person appointed by the Minister.
DECLARE ChildApplicant IS ONE OF
    `a guardian or custodian`
    `the child`
    `a sibling`
    `a Minister's appointee`

GIVEN `who applies` IS A ChildApplicant, `the child's age` IS A NUMBER, `the applicant's age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for child maintenance` IF
    CONSIDER `who applies`
    WHEN `a guardian or custodian` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Minister's appointee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the child` THEN `the child's age` >= 21
    WHEN `a sibling` THEN `the child's age` < 21 AND `the applicant's age` >= 21

-- s 69(5): no order "for the benefit of a child who has attained 21 years of age or for a period that extends beyond"
-- that day unless necessary because of (a) a mental or physical disability; (b) full-time national service;
-- (c) education or training for a trade, profession or vocation, "whether or not while in gainful employment"; or
-- (d) other special circumstances.
GIVEN `has a disability` IS A BOOLEAN, `in national service` IS A BOOLEAN, `in education or training` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `maintenance may run past age 21` IF
    `has a disability` OR `in national service` OR `in education or training` OR `special circumstances`

§§ `60, 60A, 63C -- protection orders against family violence`

-- s 60(1): "A protector may apply for a protection order against any person." (2): for family violence against Y --
-- (a) if Y is below 18: a family member of Y, Y's guardian, or a person caring for Y; (b) if Y is assessed to lack the
-- mental capacity to apply: a family member, Y's donee or deputy, or a carer; "(c) in any other case -- Y".
-- (3): "A person who is below 18 years of age may not apply for a protection order under subsection (2) unless the
-- person is married or was previously married."
-- On the literal words, Y personally may apply only under (c), so a married Y below 18 cannot apply for herself; s 60(3)
-- then reaches a married minor applying as a family member of someone else. This is a literal reading, not tested law.
DECLARE POApplicant IS ONE OF
    `the person harmed`
    `a family member`
    `a guardian, donee, deputy or carer`
    `a protector`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A POApplicant, `Y is below 18` IS A BOOLEAN, `Y lacks mental capacity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the applicant is below 18` IS A BOOLEAN, `the applicant is or was married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for a protection order` IF
    CONSIDER `the applicant`
    WHEN `a protector` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the person harmed` THEN
            (NOT `Y is below 18`) AND (NOT `Y lacks mental capacity`)
        AND ((NOT `the applicant is below 18`) OR `the applicant is or was married`)
    OTHERWISE
            (`Y is below 18` OR `Y lacks mental capacity`)
        AND ((NOT `the applicant is below 18`) OR `the applicant is or was married`)

-- s 60A(1): the court may make a protection order if satisfied "on a balance of probabilities" that (a) X "has committed
-- or is likely to commit family violence against Y"; and (b) the order "is necessary for the protection or personal
-- safety of Y". (6): knowingly contravening it is a family violence offence.
GIVEN `X has committed or is likely to commit family violence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order is necessary for Y's safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make a protection order` IF
    `X has committed or is likely to commit family violence` AND `the order is necessary for Y's safety`

-- s 63C(1): (a) aggravated -- fine up to $10,000 or up to 18 months or both; (b) otherwise up to $10,000 or 12 months or
-- both. (2): aggravated if the offence contravenes an order protecting a vulnerable adult AND the offender has a prior
-- family violence conviction for contravening the same or another order protecting a vulnerable adult.
GIVEN `the order protects a vulnerable adult` IS A BOOLEAN, `prior conviction for breaching a vulnerable adult order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment for breaching a protection order in months` IS
    IF `the order protects a vulnerable adult` AND `prior conviction for breaching a vulnerable adult order`
    THEN 18
    ELSE 12

§§ `93, 94 -- jurisdiction and the three-year bar`

-- s 93(1): the court has divorce jurisdiction only if either party is (a) "domiciled in Singapore" at commencement or
-- (b) "habitually resident in Singapore for a period of 3 years immediately preceding" commencement.
GIVEN `either party is domiciled in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `longest habitual residence in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court has divorce jurisdiction` IF
    `either party is domiciled in Singapore` OR `longest habitual residence in years` >= 3

-- s 94(1): no originating application for divorce "unless at the date of the filing ... 3 years have passed since the
-- date of the marriage". (2): the court may give permission earlier for "exceptional hardship suffered by the applicant
-- or of exceptional depravity on the part of the respondent".
GIVEN `years since the marriage` IS A NUMBER, `permission for exceptional hardship or depravity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a divorce application may be filed` IF
    `years since the marriage` >= 3 OR `permission for exceptional hardship or depravity`

§§ `95, 95A -- irretrievable breakdown`

-- s 95A(1): a marriage between X and Y has irretrievably broken down "if and only if" (a) X committed adultery and Y finds
-- it intolerable to live with X; (b) X "has behaved in such a way that Y cannot reasonably be expected to live with X";
-- (c) X deserted Y "for a continuous period of 2 or more years"; (d) they lived apart 3 or more years AND both consent;
-- (e) they lived apart 4 or more years; (f) "X and Y agree that the marriage has irretrievably broken down".
-- (2)(b): if Y lives with X "for more than 6 months" after knowing of the adultery, Y "may not rely on that act".
-- (3): for behaviour, living together 6 months or less is merely ignored -- more than 6 months is NOT a bar on the words.
-- (4), (5): desertion and living apart stay continuous if they lived together "for a total of 6 months or less", but that
-- time "does not count towards the length".
-- (6): the (f) agreement must be in writing, and "the court must not accept the agreement" if "there remains a reasonable
-- possibility that X and Y might reconcile".
-- Here X is the respondent and Y the applicant, which keeps s 95(2)(b) (not relying on one's own conduct) satisfied.
-- SIMPLIFICATION: more than 6 months together is treated as breaking the period entirely (counted as 0).
DECLARE Breakdown HAS
    `the respondent committed adultery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant finds it intolerable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months lived together after learning of it` IS A NUMBER
    `the respondent behaved so the applicant cannot reasonably live with them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of desertion` IS A NUMBER
    `months together during the desertion` IS A NUMBER
    `months living apart` IS A NUMBER
    `months together during the separation` IS A NUMBER
    `both consent to a divorce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written agreement that it has broken down` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reconciliation remains reasonably possible` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `total months` IS A NUMBER, `months together` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months that count` IS
    IF `months together` > 6 THEN 0 ELSE `total months` - `months together`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Breakdown
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the marriage has irretrievably broken down` IF
        (`the facts`'s `the respondent committed adultery`
            AND `the facts`'s `the applicant finds it intolerable`
            AND `the facts`'s `months lived together after learning of it` <= 6)
    OR  `the facts`'s `the respondent behaved so the applicant cannot reasonably live with them`
    OR  `the months that count` (`the facts`'s `months of desertion`) (`the facts`'s `months together during the desertion`) >= 24
    OR  (`the months that count` (`the facts`'s `months living apart`) (`the facts`'s `months together during the separation`) >= 36
            AND `the facts`'s `both consent to a divorce`)
    OR  `the months that count` (`the facts`'s `months living apart`) (`the facts`'s `months together during the separation`) >= 48
    OR  (`the facts`'s `a written agreement that it has broken down`
            AND (NOT `the facts`'s `reconciliation remains reasonably possible`))

-- s 95(2): a divorce "is to be granted if and only if" (a) the marriage has irretrievably broken down; (b) the applicant
-- is not relying on his or her own adultery, behaviour or desertion; and (c) "it is just and reasonable to grant the
-- divorce", having regard to the parties' conduct and how a divorce would affect them and any child. (3): otherwise the
-- court "must dismiss".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A Breakdown, `just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a divorce is to be granted` IF
    `the marriage has irretrievably broken down` `the facts` AND `just and reasonable`
